---
// Meet Lauren — magazine feature (big display name, multi-column article,
// cutout right). Copy: first-person bio pasted by JY Sep 9, verbatim.
// (Replaced the Sep 1 Celestine third-person draft — career credentials and
// the "Sign up here" enroll link went with it.) Cutout: Lauren with her two
// boys (landed Sep 9), seated group standing on the section's bottom edge.
---

<section class="fc-lauren-d" id="meet-lauren" aria-labelledby="lauren-title-d" data-nav-cream>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="article">
      <h2 id="lauren-title-d" data-rv style="--rvi: 0">Meet Lauren Kassan</h2>

      <p class="dek" data-rv style="--rvi: 1">
        Founder of STAND
      </p>

      <div class="cols" data-rv style="--rvi: 2">
        <p>
          I&rsquo;ve been an entrepreneur for most of my adult life. I
          didn&rsquo;t go to business school &mdash; I learned by doing:
          putting ideas into the world, getting things right, getting things
          wrong, and trying again. That experience taught me how to solve
          problems, trust my judgment, and carry an idea from its earliest
          stages into something real.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now, as a mother of two, I think deeply about what kids need to
          thrive in a world changing faster than schools can adapt. I created
          STAND to help kids think for themselves, solve real problems,
          understand money, communicate confidently, and use the tools of
          their generation without losing their own judgment and creativity.
          Entrepreneurship is the vehicle. The real product is the
          confidence, resourcefulness, and agency they build along the way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <img
      class="cutout"
      src="/brand/lauren-family-cutout-3.webp"
      alt="Lauren, founder and CEO of STAND, with her two sons"
      loading="lazy"
      width="1600"
      height="1509"
      data-rv
      style="--rvi: 3"
    />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .fc-lauren-d {
    background: var(--stand-cream);
    color: var(--stand-black);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    /* Family cutout gets a full half — the photo is the feature now. */
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
    align-items: end;
    max-width: calc(1440px + 2 * 48px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(48px, 5.5vw, 88px) 48px 0;
  }

  .article {
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 5.5vw, 88px);
  }

  /* The reference's big display name, top-left. */
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 6.4vw, 100px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--stand-red);
  }

  .dek {
    margin: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 26px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .dek em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--stand-red);
  }

  /* Magazine columns: small dense article text. */
  .cols {
    margin-top: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 32px);
    columns: 2;
    column-gap: clamp(36px, 3.6vw, 64px);
  }

  .cols p {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    /* Same size as the Location week-table rows. */
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.4vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Full-height cutout standing on the section's bottom edge. */
  .cutout {
    display: block;
    width: min(100%, 656px);
    height: auto;
    justify-self: center;
    align-self: end;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-left: 20px;
      padding-right: 20px;
    }

    .article {
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .cols {
      columns: 1;
    }

    .cutout {
      width: min(70%, 300px);
    }
  }
</style>
